    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0677" n="667" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg667"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11–2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Robertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-24T14:00:00+07:00">November 24,
                            1945—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 24—1:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2029. In telegram dated November 20 Secretary Stevens<anchor n="66"
                        xml:id="d493-f1"/> at Peiping reports in substance as follows:</p>
                <p>Military information covering last 3 weeks reflects progressive deterioration of
                    Central Government’s military position vis-à-vis Chinese Communists in North
                    China. Communists are concentrated along the eastern part of Great Wall,
                    especially at passes, resulting in serious disorders in Chahar and Suiyuan, and
                    along Peiping-Liaoning and Peiping-Suiyuan railways. Communists have repeatedly
                    destroyed sections of Peiping-Liaoning Railway between Chinwangtao and Kailan
                    coal fields. Coal trains guarded by U.S. Marines and Marine plane[s?] have been
                    fired on in this region. Communists’ siege of Kueisui intensified during first 2
                    weeks of November and Communist advance on Paotou under way. Communist activity
                    is also reported on <pb facs="0678" n="668" xml:id="pg668"/> Honan-Hopeh border.
                    The Peiping area is calm, with Communists controlling hills believed to be only
                    Communist militia. Commodity prices continue to advance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
